The application jar bundles third-party libraries under permissive licenses, checked at build
time against config/allowed-licenses.json (./gradlew checkLicense), notably:
  - Spring Boot, Spring Framework, Micrometer, Flyway, HikariCP (Apache-2.0)
  - Jackson (Apache-2.0)
  - ASM (BSD-3-Clause)
  - PostgreSQL JDBC driver (BSD-2-Clause)
  - JSpecify (Apache-2.0)

The container image additionally installs, as separate executables that are never linked to
this code:
  - GuardDog (Datadog, Apache-2.0) and its Python dependencies, including pygit2
    (GPL-2.0 with linking exception)
  - malcontent (Chainguard, Apache-2.0), run with --third-party=false: third-party YARA rules
    under other licenses are not used unless a deployment enables them knowingly.
